# 9. Ingredient Intelligence

The Ingredient Intelligence Engine converts messy food information into structured information.

It should identify:

- Direct ingredients
- Ingredient synonyms
- Derived ingredients
- Hidden/indirect ingredient relationships
- Allergens
- Additives
- Nutritionally relevant ingredients
- Ambiguous ingredients
- Unspecified ingredient sources

### Examples

| Ingredient | Interpretation |
|---|---|
| Casein | Milk-derived |
| Whey | Milk-derived |
| Lactose | Milk-derived |
| Maltodextrin | Carbohydrate-related |
| Gluten | Relevant to gluten/wheat restrictions |
| Peanut powder | Peanut-derived |
| Vegetable protein | Source may require verification |

The system should maintain confidence for ingredient interpretations.

